🔍 Splunk SPL Detection Queries

This document contains the core Search Processing Language (SPL) queries used in this lab to detect, investigate, and visualize the simulated brute-force attack and AWS anomalies.

1. High-Velocity Brute Force Detection (Basic Alert)

Purpose: Detects an excessive number of failed SSH login attempts from a single source IP address within a short timeframe.
Threshold: > 10 failures in 5 minutes.

index=aws_ec2_logs sourcetype=linux_secure action=failure
| bin _time span=5m
| stats count by _time, src_ip, user
| where count > 10
| eval Threat_Level="High", Status="Brute Force Attempt Detected"
| table _time, src_ip, user, count, Threat_Level, Status
| sort - count


2. Successful Compromise: Login Following Brute Force (Critical Alert)

Purpose: Identifies if an attacker successfully guessed a password and logged in after generating multiple failed attempts. This is a critical incident response trigger.

index=aws_ec2_logs sourcetype=linux_secure (action=failure OR action=success)
| transaction src_ip maxspan=10m
| search action=failure AND action=success
| stats count(eval(action="failure")) as Failed_Attempts, count(eval(action="success")) as Successful_Logins by src_ip, user, _time
| where Failed_Attempts > 5 AND Successful_Logins > 0
| eval Alert="CRITICAL: Successful Authentication Post-Brute Force"
| table _time, src_ip, user, Failed_Attempts, Successful_Logins, Alert


3. Threat Intelligence & Geo-Location Mapping (Dashboard Visualization)

Purpose: Extracts the IP addresses of failed logins and maps them geographically. This query is designed to be used with Splunk's Choropleth Map visualization on a SOC dashboard.

index=aws_ec2_logs sourcetype=linux_secure action=failure
| iplocation src_ip
| stats count by Country, City, src_ip
| where Country != "United States" 
| sort - count
| geostats count by Country


4. AWS CloudTrail: Suspicious IAM Activity (Lateral Movement/Persistence)

Purpose: Monitors AWS CloudTrail logs to detect if the compromised EC2 instance (or the attacker) attempts to create new IAM users or attach administrative policies, indicating a persistence mechanism.

index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype=aws:cloudtrail (eventName=CreateUser OR eventName=AttachUserPolicy OR eventName=AttachGroupPolicy)
| stats count by _time, eventName, requestParameters.userName, sourceIPAddress, userAgent
| rename requestParameters.userName as Target_User, sourceIPAddress as Source_IP
| eval Mitigation="Review IAM permissions immediately and revoke unauthorized access"
| table _time, eventName, Target_User, Source_IP, userAgent, Mitigation
